<VI _name="lvdqmh_wire_module_data.vi" description="Connects the handler subVI of ONE message frame of a DQMH Main.vi to the module's DATA CLUSTER - the cluster the Message Handling Loop carries in its shift register (Module Data--cluster.ctl) - BY FIELD NAME, the way the Hampel Soft DQMH conventions want module state kept\3A on the MHL shift register, never in a functional global variable.\0A\0AFINDING THE DATA WIRE\3A of the frame's Case Structure tunnels, the INPUT tunnel whose outside wire comes from a shift register (an owner class matching ShiftRegister) is the data cluster - the message, its data and the error come from Dequeue. Its inside terminal in this frame is Data In\3B the one sink of that wire, an output tunnel, is Data Out. Pass Through is TRUE when the frame does nothing with the data yet (one wire, straight to the output tunnel).\0A\0AREAD FIELDS\3A an Unbundle By Name, copied from the Donor VI with Move (duplicate TRUE) - VI Server's New VI Object cannot create one (Error 1054, measured 2026-11-12) - is wired to Data In and its outputs to the handler inputs named in Read Terminals (pairwise - the tool names them `&lt;field&gt; in`). WRITE FIELDS\3A the pass-through wire is deleted, a Bundle By Name copied the same way takes Data In as its input cluster and the handler outputs named in Write Terminals (pairwise - `&lt;field&gt; out`), and its output goes to Data Out\3B a field the handler does not output is never written back. The Donor VI is GENERATED for the call, with nodes that already carry exactly these field names. Move with duplicate answers the ORIGINAL's reference, so the copy is found in the frame as the node of its class whose input cluster (Unbundle) or output cluster (Bundle) is still unwired.\0A\0AWith Dry Run TRUE nothing changes and the answer says what was found. Main.vi is reached in the ACTIVE PROJECT's application instance and saved in place. Requires lvbd_connect_by_names.vi, lvbd_terminal_by_name.vi and lvbd_move_to.vi to be open when this VI is generated.">
